go 1.26.0

// Local multi-module workspace: the desktop app and the CLI both build against
// the shared engine in ./cli/engine without needing it published. This
// workspace is ACTIVE for every build, including goreleaser's, so desktop/'s
// module graph participates in resolving the released CLI binary. The replace
// directive in desktop/go.mod would make GOWORK=off work, but nothing uses it.
//
// The go line above moves by hand. Dependabot raises the go line of cli/go.mod
// or desktop/go.mod when a dependency needs a newer Go, but never this one, and
// every Go command then stops with "module . listed in go.work file requires
// go >= X, but go.work lists go Y" (#504 sat red for that reason). Move all
// three together, with the Go floor quoted in CONTRIBUTING.md, DESKTOP.md,
// docs/cli/installation.mdx, docs/reference/architecture.mdx and
// client/public/install.sh.
//
// The go-version pins in .github/workflows/ are a separate line: the toolchain
// CI and the releases build with, which may be newer than this floor. Since
// 2026-10-16 they are 1.27 while the floor stays 1.26.0 (the owner's
// decision), so a source build on 1.26 still works: on macOS 12, which Go 1.27
// dropped, that is the only route. The floor also sets the GODEBUG defaults:
// a go1.27.2 build of floe carries DefaultGODEBUG=tracebacklabels=0,
// x509sslcertoverrideplatform=0, the 1.26 behavior of both settings 1.27
// changed. Raising the floor to 1.27 changes those defaults and lets
// writePartial's lock go (cli/engine/transfer/partial.go).
use (
	./cli
	./desktop
)
